        "title": "Structuralism and the Prague School",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Structuralism is the application of Saussure's linguistic methodology — the study of signs as relational systems of differences — to domains beyond language: myth, kinship, unconscious, literature, culture. Its core claim is that beneath the surface of phenomena lies an underlying structure (a system of oppositions and rules) that generates the surface forms."
    },
