        "title": "Structuralism and the Prague School",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Prague School (Prague Linguistic Circle, 1926–1948) was the first major institutional application of Saussurean ideas. It made fundamental contributions to phonology, the theory of functions of language, and the poetics of language."
